> Adaptive Dormand–Prince and Adams work

RK45 computes fifth- and embedded fourth-order proposals with seven actual RHS
evaluations per trial. Although the tableau permits FSAL reuse, this
implementation does not reuse the final stage. Its actual scaled RMS error is

$$ E=\sqrt{\frac1D\sum_{i=1}^{D}\left(\frac{y_i^{(5)}-y_i^{(4)}}{a_{tol}+r_{tol}\max(|y_i|,|y_i^{(5)}|)}\right)^2}. $$
\alttext(The adaptive error is the root mean square of componentwise embedded differences divided by positive absolute-plus-relative scales.)

Accept only E≤1. The next trial step is multiplied by clamp(.9 E^(−1/5),.2,5),
with growth5 when E=0, then bounded by max_step and remaining interval. Rejected
trials still cost seven callbacks. Unsafe normalization arithmetic uses a
recorded wider route; a local embedded criterion does not certify global error.
The old unconditional acceptance of tiny steps with E>1 has been removed.

Adams-Bashforth uses previously accepted derivatives. At order4,

$$ y_{pred}=y_n+\frac h{24}(55f_n-59f_{n-1}+37f_{n-2}-9f_{n-3}). $$
\alttext(The fourth-order explicit Adams predictor combines the four most recent derivatives with coefficients55,minus59,37,minus9 divided by24.)

The Adams-Moulton option performs one PECE correction,

$$ y_{next}=y_n+\frac h{24}(9f(t_{n+1},y_{pred})+19f_n-5f_{n-1}+f_{n-2}). $$
\alttext(The corrector uses one derivative at the predicted next state together with three stored derivatives; it is one correction, not an iterated nonlinear solve.)

Orders2through4 use their corresponding coefficients; the original order control
is clamped to that range. RK4 supplies startup history. Constant-grid formulas
are not applied blindly to a shortened final step: that tail now uses RK4. The
method is not a full Newton-solved implicit integrator or a general stiff
solver.

> Retain all original decay comparisons

The native comparison helper preserves y'=−y,y(0)=1,t∈[0,2],
Euler/midpoint/RK4/AB4/PECE4 at nominal h=.01, and RK45 initial h=.1 with
absolute/relative tolerances1e−8. A second native helper preserves the original
step sweep. Each row retains actual accepted steps and callbacks, so
endpoint-tail handling, startup costs and rejection costs remain visible rather
than hard-coded to old counts.

The extra coarse-initial-step adaptive control is separate from the original
comparison: it deliberately starts at h=2 with tolerances1e−12, exposing actual
rejected trials. Its count comes from actual trial records.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ode_decay.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto comparison = dm::ode::ode_decay_comparison();
    auto sweep = dm::ode::ode_decay_step_study();
    std::vector<std::string> names;
    std::vector<double> cost;
    std::print("| original method | actual final y | closed-form absolute error | actual accepted steps | " "actual callbacks | actual final time |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : comparison) {
        names.push_back(r.name);
        cost.push_back(r.solution.function_evaluations);
        std::print("| {} | {:.15f} | {:.8e} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.name,
                   r.solution.y.back()[0], r.absolute_error,
                   r.solution.steps_taken, r.solution.function_evaluations,
                   r.solution.t.back());
    }
    std::vector<double> x, euler, rk4;
    std::print("\n| original nominal step | actual Euler endpoint error | actual RK4 endpoint error | " "actual Euler steps | actual RK4 steps |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : sweep) {
        x.push_back(std::log10(r.step));
        euler.push_back(std::log10(std::max(r.euler_error, 1e-18)));
        rk4.push_back(std::log10(std::max(r.rk4_error, 1e-18)));
        std::print("| {} | {:.8e} | {:.8e} | {} | {} |\n", r.step,
                   r.euler_error, r.rk4_error, r.euler_steps, r.rk4_steps);
    }
    auto adaptive =
        dm::ode::ODESolver({dm::ode::StepMethod::RK45, 4, 2., 1e-12, 1e-12, 0}).trace_builtin("exponential_decay", {1.}, {1.}, 0, 2);
    std::print("\nSeparate coarse adaptive control: {} actual trials, {} accepted, {} rejected, {} actual " "callbacks.\n",
               adaptive.attempts.size(), adaptive.solution.steps_taken,
               adaptive.attempts.size() - adaptive.solution.steps_taken,
               adaptive.solution.function_evaluations);
    auto errors = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    errors.lines(x, euler, "Euler", dm::graphics::RGBA{220, 38, 38, 255}).points(x, euler, dm::graphics::RGBA{220, 38, 38, 255}, 3.).lines(x, rk4, "RK4", dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255}).points(x, rk4, dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255}, 3.);
    errors.title("Actual global endpoint error at t=2").x_label(
        "log10(nominal step)").y_label("log10(max(actual endpoint error,1e-18))");
    auto calls = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(cost, names, "actual RHS calls");
    calls.title("Original six methods: actual RHS work").x_label(
        "original method configuration").y_label("actual derivative callbacks");
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 1);
    layout.size(1100, 1200).add(errors).add(calls).fit_panels().save_svg(
        "build/ode_decay.svg");
}
```
