> Original harmonic oscillator and scaled energy drift

For omega1, x'=v,v'=−x with initial[1,0], the exact solution is
x=cos(t),v=−sin(t). The original RK4 h=.01 interval[0,20] is retained. The
scaled energy x²+v² equals1 in exact arithmetic. Classical RK4 is not symplectic
and does not enforce this invariant; the native study reports actual sampled
drift and state error instead of claiming energy preservation.

The lower panel multiplies the raw scaled-energy departure by10^12 for readable
ticks. Raw departures remain in the computed table, and the scaling is
explicitly a display transformation. This finite nonstiff example does not
establish long-time stability or universal conservation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ode_oscillator.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto s = dm::ode::ode_harmonic_study();
    auto states = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    states.lines(s.solution.t, s.position, "actual x",
                 dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255}).lines(
        s.solution.t, s.velocity, "actual v",
        dm::graphics::RGBA{220, 38, 38, 255});
    states.title("Original oscillator: actual x and v").x_label(
        "actual retained time").y_label("actual state component").y_limits(
        -1.2, 1.3);
    std::vector<double> scaled;
    for (double value : s.energy_drift)
        scaled.push_back(value * 1e12);
    auto energy = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    energy.lines(s.solution.t, scaled, "scaled actual drift",
                 dm::graphics::RGBA{22, 163, 74, 255});
    energy.title("Actual scaled-energy departure, multiplied by1e12").x_label(
        "actual retained time").y_label("1e12 times (x*x+v*v-1)");
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 1);
    layout.size(1100, 1200).add(states).add(energy).fit_panels().save_svg(
        "build/ode_oscillator.svg");
    std::print("| actual diagnostic | computed value |\n| --- | ---: |\n| final x | {:.15f} |\n| cos(20) " "reference | {:.15f} |\n| final v | {:.15f} |\n| -sin(20) reference | {:.15f} |\n| actual " "final scaled energy | {:.15f} |\n| maximum absolute raw sampled energy drift | {:.8e} |\n| " "maximum sampled state error norm | {:.8e} |\n| actual accepted steps | {} |\n| actual " "callbacks | {} |\n",
               s.position.back(), std::cos(20.), s.velocity.back(),
               -std::sin(20.), s.final_energy, s.max_energy_drift,
               s.max_state_error, s.solution.steps_taken,
               s.solution.function_evaluations);
}
```
