> Original Lorenz portrait, complete forward contracts

The original Lorenz system uses sigma10,rho28,beta8/3, initial[1,1,1], RK4
h=.005 over[0,25]:

$$ x'=10(y-x), \qquad y'=x(28-z)-y, \qquad z'=xy-(8/3)z. $$
\alttext(The Lorenz derivatives use the original parameters10,28 and eight thirds.)

All returned samples, including the initial transient, remain in the x–z
portrait. This finite numerical path illustrates the system’s geometry; a
familiar portrait does not certify pointwise long-time accuracy or prove an
attractor. Chaotic sensitivity and fixed-step error remain separate from
successful finite integration.

Complete controls, finite nonempty initial state, finite forward span and
builtin dimensions/parameters are checked before callbacks. Every stage and
returned derivative must remain finite and fixed-dimensional. Nonadvancing
representable time throws. The old absolute1e−14 endpoint skip is removed, so
even a smaller positive interval is integrated; successful trajectories include
the exact requested terminal time. This can change the final tail and reported
counts from the old report. Callback effects before a later failure cannot be
rolled back, and no partial solution/trace is returned.

Default execution limits are1000000 actual attempts,7000000 callbacks and1000000
retained solution time/state scalars. Explicit limits overloads allow zero to
disable each policy. Trace admission counts original options/times8+initial
dimensionD, accepted samples1+D, callbacks2+2D and trials1+2D. The default trace
cap is1000000 logical units, zero disabling; record metadata, capacities and
allocator cost are excluded. Ordinary work follows actual callbacks/state
algebra and retains every accepted trajectory state; trace storage additionally
follows every actual callback/trial. No shared mutable solver state or retained
caller references are introduced.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ode_lorenz.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto s = dm::ode::ode_lorenz_study();
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(s.x, s.z, "actual full trajectory",
            dm::graphics::RGBA{124, 58, 237, 255});
    p.title("Original Lorenz run: full x-z phase portrait").x_label("actual x").y_label("actual z").save_svg("build/ode_lorenz.svg");
    std::print("| actual original Lorenz quantity | computed value |\n| --- | --- |\n| accepted steps | {} " "|\n| derivative callbacks | {} |\n| first retained time | {} |\n| last retained time | {} " "|\n| final actual state | `{}` |\n",
               s.solution.steps_taken, s.solution.function_evaluations,
               s.solution.t.front(), s.solution.t.back(), s.solution.y.back());
    auto tiny =
        dm::ode::ODESolver().solve_builtin("exponential_decay", {1.}, {1.}, 0,
                                           1e-16);
    std::print("\nPositive tiny-interval control: {} actual retained samples, actual final time {:.17e}, " "actual callbacks {}.\n",
               tiny.size(), tiny.t.back(), tiny.function_evaluations);
}
```
